; background-findv-expanded.scm as basic blocks, called from the top level.
; The call (pred v i) is written as the opaque test pred(v, i), declared in the slide's prims, so
; that the drawing stays small; it tells nothing about v or i.
; The caller tests the result of findv before using it as an index: (fixnum? arg) is the test
; that Lambda Versioning removes, since findv only returns #f or a fixnum.
; The slide runs it with intervals (no symbolic vector bounds, as on the abstract interpretation
; slide): ##vector-length returns at most maxfix, so i < len keeps i + 1 a fixnum and the overflow
; fallback of fx+? is never reached. Without intervals, that fallback makes i a fx | bg and the
; exit site of R returns fx | bg, so the (fixnum? arg) test would stay.
function main()
M:  v = read()
    call findv(v) -> C
C:  arg = #res
    if vector?(v) goto D else goto K
D:  if fixnum?(arg) goto E else goto K
E:  if fx>=(arg, 0) goto F else goto K
F:  len = ##vector-length(v)
    if fx<(arg, len) goto G else goto K
G:  return ##vector-ref(v, arg)
K:  fail

function findv(v)
A:  goto L(i=0)
L:  if vector?(v) goto M else goto K
K:  fail
M:  len = ##vector-length(v)
    if >=(i, len) goto N else goto P
N:  return #f
P:  if pred(v, i) goto R else goto S
R:  return i
S:  if fixnum?(i) goto T else goto U
T:  i2 = fx+?(i, 1)
    if i2 goto T2 else goto O
T2: goto L(i=i2)
O:  i3 = ##+(i, 1)
    goto L(i=i3)
U:  if flonum?(i) goto W else goto X
W:  i4 = fl+(i, 1.0)
    goto L(i=i4)
X:  i5 = ##+(i, 1)
    goto L(i=i5)
